# --- Data (raw, interim, processed, external) ---
# The data/ directory must never carry real or downloaded datasets in version
# control. Only data/README.md and data/metadata/ (provenance records, no
# actual data) are versioned - see data/README.md for the full layout.
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/.gitkeep
!data/metadata/
data/metadata/*
!data/metadata/source_registry.yaml
!data/metadata/dataset_roles.yaml
!data/metadata/file_manifest.csv
!data/metadata/schemas/
data/metadata/schemas/*
!data/metadata/schemas/*.yaml
!data/metadata/licenses/
data/metadata/licenses/*
!data/metadata/licenses/*.md
!data/metadata/licenses/*.txt
*.csv
!data/metadata/file_manifest.csv
# Small, deliberately artificial contract-validation fixtures (never real
# or acquired data - see tests/fixtures/contracts/ and docs/data_contracts.md)
# must stay versioned; the blanket *.csv rule above exists to keep real/
# acquired data out of git, not to hide test fixtures from it. Discovered
# as a real, previously-silent gap during Phase 4A - see this phase's
# final report.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.csv
# dbt seeds are, by dbt's own convention, checked into version control
# (small, static reference/dimension data, never real or acquired data
# - see warehouse/seeds/dim_dpd_bucket.csv itself). The blanket *.csv
# rule above silently caught this one too - confirmed as a real,
# 100%-reproducible-on-Linux dbt compilation error ("depends on a node
# named 'dim_dpd_bucket' which was not found") on a genuinely fresh
# clone, since the seed CSV was never committed despite the dbt model
# that declares/patches it (models/dimensions/_dimensions__models.yml)
# being tracked all along.
!warehouse/seeds/*.csv
# Fase 11C Gate D - the OFFICIAL model's own frozen split assignment
# (which UCI rows are train/validation/test) and the small classifier-
# threshold summary table it needs are both load-bearing INPUTS to
# monitoring reference reconstruction (credlens.monitoring.reference.
# build_reference / credlens.monitoring.runner._top10_threshold), not
# generated demo data - confirmed as a real, direct blocker of
# `credlens monitor evaluate-detection` on a genuinely fresh clone
# (FileNotFoundError for both, reproduced in a real clean-room tree).
# Small (403 KB / 1.3 KB) and deterministic given the already-frozen
# EXP_behavioral_default_v1 experiment - the same "small, static,
# never-real-acquired-data" category as warehouse/seeds/dim_dpd_bucket.
# csv above, not the bulkier per-row prediction tables this same
# directory also holds (those stay gitignored - regenerable via
# `credlens model evaluate`, and genuinely bulk generated output, not a
# frozen reference constant). Committed in Fase 11C/11D.
!reports/modeling/experiments/*/split_assignment.csv
!reports/modeling/tables/*__thresholds.csv
# Fase 11D - same category as the two exceptions above: a small (19
# rows, ~5 KB), deterministic, per-FEATURE (never per-individual)
# summary of the already-frozen EXP_behavioral_default_v1 model's
# coefficient-stability classification, read by production code
# (credlens.model_validation.remediation/reporting), not just a test
# fixture. Confirmed missing on a genuinely fresh clean-room clone,
# breaking tests/test_model_validation_remediation.py - the same
# blanket `*.csv` rule silently caught it too. No PII, no raw/acquired
# data, no individual-level rows - only aggregate statistics over the
# already-licensed (CC BY 4.0) UCI benchmark's engineered features.
!reports/model_validation/tables/*__coefficient_classification.csv
# Fase 11E - same category and same directory as the exception directly
# above: a tiny (9-19 rows, <1 KB each), deterministic, per-FEATURE
# (never per-individual) VIF (variance inflation factor) table, read
# unconditionally by production code (credlens.model_validation.
# remediation.compare_five_models, via `credlens model remediate`) for
# the already-frozen EXP_behavioral_default_v1 model - not just a test
# fixture. Confirmed as a real, direct blocker on a genuine GitHub
# Actions Linux runner: tests/test_model_validation_remediation.py::
# TestCliRemediate::test_cli_remediate_and_compare failed with
# FileNotFoundError on a fresh checkout because the blanket `*.csv` rule
# silently caught this one too, exactly like the coefficient-
# classification table before it. No PII, no raw/acquired data, no
# individual-level rows - only aggregate VIF statistics over the
# already-licensed (CC BY 4.0) UCI benchmark's engineered features. The
# v2_reduced/v2_reduced_stability_only siblings are the already-computed,
# equally small outputs of the same completed Gate D remediation
# exercise as their already-tracked *__coefficient_classification.csv
# counterparts, so this exception (like that one) is left general to the
# directory rather than pinned to the v1 filename only.
!reports/model_validation/tables/*__vif.csv
# Fase 11E - the portfolio-analysis layer's own official, versioned
# output tables (aggregate business metrics only - run_id/suite_id/
# scenario/month grain, never a customer/contract-level row; largest is
# 1.3 MB, 1.6 MB total for all 12) were caught by the blanket `*.csv`
# rule too, even though every OTHER file this same `credlens analysis
# run` invocation writes to reports/portfolio_analysis/ (insights.yml,
# manifest.json, the bilingual reports, the *.png figures) was already
# committed. Confirmed as a real, direct blocker on a genuine GitHub
# Actions Linux runner (reproduced identically in WSL): the committed,
# versioned case-study notebook (notebooks/credit_portfolio_case_study.
# ipynb) reads these tables directly and fails with FileNotFoundError
# without them - this is deliberately-versioned analysis evidence for
# the notebook to demonstrate against, not scratch/regenerable CI-build
# output (that lives under data/warehouse/, already covered by data/*
# above). No PII, no real/acquired data - entirely synthetic portfolio
# metrics. Scoped to this exact directory only, never a blanket
# unignore of CSVs elsewhere.
!reports/portfolio_analysis/tables/*.csv
*.tsv
*.parquet
*.feather
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.zip
*.7z
*.gz
*.asc

