# --- Logs ---
*.log
logs/

# --- Dashboard demo package (Phase 7 / Fase 11C Gate B) ---
# `credlens demo prepare --component dashboard` (src/credlens/demo/
# factory.py) deterministically regenerates the ENTIRE demo bundle
# (Parquet tables + manifest.json + insights.yml) from a seed - the
# dashboard's own --demo mode now auto-generates it in-process the
# first time it's needed (credlens.dashboard.bootstrap), so nothing
# under here needs to be committed for the dashboard demo to work from
# a fresh clone. manifest.json/insights.yml were tracked from before
# this factory existed, orphaned once the *.parquet tables they
# reference became gitignored (Fase 11C) - a real, confirmed regression
# on a genuinely fresh clone (Fase 11D): `_skip_if_absent()`-style test
# guards see manifest.json present and proceed, then fail with
# "Demo table 'X' is missing" since its parquets were never committed.
# Fase 11D `git rm --cached` both, closing the gap the auto-generation
# above already exists to fill.
dashboard/demo_data/*

# --- Jupyter (Phase 7 notebook extra) ---
# Checkpoint files and an ad hoc executed-notebook copy are transient
# evidence of a `jupyter nbconvert --execute` run, never the source
# notebook itself (notebooks/*.ipynb IS versioned).
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*_executed.ipynb

# --- Modeling (Phase 8: behavioral early-warning model) ---
# Per-experiment working model artifacts (one .joblib per model kind per
# `credlens model train` run) are fully reproducible from the same
# --experiment-id/--seed (see reports/modeling/README.md) and grow with
# every experiment - never versioned. Only the curated, gate-passed
# candidate under reports/modeling/models/*.joblib (+ its .manifest.json)
# is versioned - small, deliberate, analogous to a champion reference
# artifact, not a scratch directory.
reports/modeling/experiments/*/models/

# Fase 11B Gate B: one quarantine manifest per local run that exercised
# input-contract quarantine handling (721 accidentally-tracked files
# found - see reports/release/tracked_cleanup_manifest.json) - fully
# reproducible, never curated release content.
reports/modeling/quarantine/

# --- Model validation (Phase 9: independent validation) ---
# The frozen evidence manifest carries a `frozen_at_utc` timestamp and is
# purely an internal integrity-check artifact (hashes already duplicated,
# in stable form, across decision.json/validation_report.md and the
# gitignored CSV tables) - never versioned, always regenerable via
# `credlens model validate-independent`.
reports/model_validation/evidence/

# --- Monitoring (Phase 9: production monitoring simulation) ---
# Fase 11B Gate B: one alert log and one run record per local
# monitoring-pipeline invocation (164 + 138 accidentally-tracked files
# found - see reports/release/tracked_cleanup_manifest.json) - fully
# reproducible via `credlens monitor run`/`evaluate`, never curated
# release content.
reports/monitoring/alerts/
# Fase 11C Gate D: `credlens demo prepare --component monitoring`
# (src/credlens/demo/factory.py) now deterministically regenerates the
# reference (REF_<model_id>.json/__population.csv/__alert_thresholds.
# json) and the simulated batch set (BATCHSET_<reference_id>/, incl.
# batch_manifest.json) from the already-committed, already-frozen
# official model - superseding Fase 11B's decision to keep
# BATCHSET_REF_MODEL_behavioral_default_v1/batch_manifest.json tracked
# as "load-bearing" (true at the time; no regeneration path existed
# yet). reports/monitoring/reference/REF_MODEL_behavioral_default_v1.
# json and its __alert_thresholds.json sibling are CURRENTLY still
# tracked from before this factory existed - removing them from the
# index is a deliberate act for a human to authorize (git rm --cached),
# not something this phase's own "no index changes" rule permits doing
# automatically; this rule only prevents a FUTURE regeneration from
# being accidentally re-tracked. The exceptions below are NOT an
# oversight - see the identical dashboard/demo_data/ comment above for
# why an ignore rule that still matches an already-tracked path breaks
# credlens.release.staging's dry-run tooling.
reports/monitoring/reference/*
!reports/monitoring/reference/REF_MODEL_behavioral_default_v1.json
!reports/monitoring/reference/REF_MODEL_behavioral_default_v1__alert_thresholds.json
reports/monitoring/runs/*
!reports/monitoring/runs/BATCHSET_REF_MODEL_behavioral_default_v1/
reports/monitoring/runs/BATCHSET_REF_MODEL_behavioral_default_v1/*
!reports/monitoring/runs/BATCHSET_REF_MODEL_behavioral_default_v1/batch_manifest.json

# --- Warehouse (Phase 5: DuckDB + dbt) ---
# warehouse/ itself (SQL/YAML/macros/seeds/analyses/tests) IS versioned -
# only dbt's own generated/compiled artifacts and the rendered profile
# (which credlens.warehouse renders from profiles.example.yml at build
# time) are excluded. The actual .duckdb database files are already
# covered by the global *.duckdb rule above and are written under
# data/warehouse/ (already covered by data/* above), never under warehouse/.
warehouse/target/
warehouse/dbt_packages/
warehouse/profiles.yml
warehouse/.user.yml
